---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<Base title="Terms of Service" description="Terms for using Aegis and the paid services from Rinse Repeat Labs.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Terms of <em>Service.</em>" lede="Draft for review. Last updated September 2026." />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow prose">
      <p class="notice">This is a working draft written by the product team. It has not yet been reviewed by counsel and will be replaced before launch.</p>
      <h2>The software</h2>
      <p>The Aegis vault is open-source software licensed under MIT or Apache-2.0, at your option. Those licences govern the software itself, including any copy you self-host.</p>
      <h2>Paid services</h2>
      <p>Personal, Family, Teams and Enterprise plans are subscriptions to hosted services: encrypted sync, encrypted backup, sharing infrastructure and support. Subscriptions renew until cancelled. Annual plans may be refunded within 30 days of purchase.</p>
      <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Choose a strong passphrase and keep your Recovery Kit and recovery secret safe, in separate places. We cannot reset any of them.</li>
        <li>Do not use the service to store or share material you have no right to.</li>
        <li>Keep your billing account credentials confidential.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Our responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Operate the relay so that it never requires or receives plaintext vault data.</li>
        <li>Publish security advisories and changes to subprocessors.</li>
        <li>Meet the support response times for your plan.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>No recovery, by design</h2>
      <p>Because we hold no key to your vault, losing your passphrase and either your Recovery Kit or its recovery secret means the vault cannot be recovered, by us or by anyone else.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p><a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
